  "comment": "**What it does**\n**Growth at a discount that the market has started to notice** - the classic PEG plus momentum recipe.\n\n- **The core test** - forward PEG at or below 1.0. You are paying less than one times next year's expected earnings growth.\n- **Real growth** - 10%+ forward EPS growth, so a low PEG is not just a collapsing denominator.\n- **Trustworthy numbers** - at least 3 analysts covering, and profitable today.\n- **Moving** - RS Rank 70+ and above the 200-day line.\n- **Moderate risk** - daily moves under 5.5%.\n\n**One change from your brief**: you asked for RS Rank 60+ AND a ~30-150 name list. Those two conflicted - at 60 the screen returned **227**. You chose to raise the momentum floor to **70**, which gives **149** and keeps every other number exactly as briefed.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- **Want the original wider net?** Drop `rs_rank` back to 60 and accept ~227 names; sorting by momentum still floats the best to the top.\n- **Want a tighter shortlist?** `rs_rank >= 80` gives ~73.\n- **Want stronger conviction?** Add `eps_revision_1m > 0` - analysts actively raising their numbers. That alone would have gotten you to ~147.\n- **Want cheaper?** Tighten `forward_peg` to 0.8, but that drifts from 'around 1' toward deep value.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `momentum_score`** - the 'market has noticed' half of the thesis.\n- **Tiebreak on `value_score`** - among equally-moving names, take the cheaper one.\n- **Avoid `income_score`** - dividends are irrelevant to this screen.\n- **Worth a look**: sort by `forward_peg` ascending for the purest GARP reading.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find growth at a discount that the market has started to notice \u2014 the \"value on\nthe move\" recipe (PEG with estimated growth plus momentum).\n- **Goal**: growth at a reasonable price. **Dividends**: ignore.\n- **The core test**: forward PEG around 1 or below \u2014 paying less than the growth\n  rate for next year's expected earnings growth (10%+).\n- **Moving**: decent price strength already (RS Rank 60+), above the 200-day line.\n- **Trustworthy estimates**: at least 3 analysts covering. Profitable companies.\n- **Size**: $500M and bigger. **Kinds**: normal stocks plus banks and insurance.\n- **Risk**: moderate. **Results**: ~30-150 names.\n- **Sorting**: momentum first, tiebreak value.",
